      "writtenOn": "2019-11-01T21:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For C code we\u0027ve started tracking the dynamic dependencies of prebuilts.  Would it make sense to leave the dependencies, since the prebuilts likely depend on the standard libs?",
      "revId": "0ef24aad03f1931eef866e6410bef2cb97b02ed8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2544d7f0_4fe33e9b",
        "filename": "rust/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-04T23:21:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the only prebuilts we use *are* stdlibs, in the form of the host sysroot. It is unlikely we will ever have any other kind of rust prebuilt, since rust libraries must be built with the *exact* revision of the compiler in use to be guaranteed to work - breakage is allowed even between different compiler build flags or patch versions.\n\nIf you\u0027d like, I could propagate this to the .bp files in prebuilts/rust instead of adding it dynamically here.",
      "parentUuid": "ad6ee49e_06eecc06",
      "tag": "autogenerated:gerrit:newPatchSet",
      "revId": "0ef24aad03f1931eef866e6410bef2cb97b02ed8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
